WEBVTT

NOTE reviewing-changes: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.476
Read the push dialog
properly before you send:

V0-2
00:00:05.576 --> 00:00:08.600
two lists, two columns,
and one count that matters.

V1a-1
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:17.028
The button carries the number of enabled
stations whose percent adjustment

V1a-2
00:00:17.128 --> 00:00:20.897
differs from what Lynx holds,
leaving out any already pushed today.

V1b-1
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.583
It is disabled when nothing is queued,

V1b-2
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.853
so a greyed-out button means
there is nothing to review.

V2a-1
00:00:33.457 --> 00:00:37.297
The left column is what Lynx holds now;
the right is what will replace it.

V2b-1
00:00:37.857 --> 00:00:42.087
Both name the station, so you are always
comparing the same head across the row.

V3a-1
00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:53.646
Available to Push comes first, ticked.
Pushed Today follows, unticked,

V3a-2
00:00:53.746 --> 00:00:57.930
and is there to stop you adjusting
the same head twice in a day.

V3b-1
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.323
That hold releases at
midnight where the course is,

V3b-2
00:01:01.423 --> 00:01:05.580
not 24 hours after the push. Tick a
pushed station only when you mean to.

V4a-1
00:01:13.243 --> 00:01:14.851
When a minimum threshold is set,

V4a-2
00:01:14.951 --> 00:01:17.313
the banner counts the
stations it will rewrite.

V4b-1
00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:21.887
The affected rows show both the original
and the value that will actually be sent.

V5a-1
00:01:28.363 --> 00:01:30.863
The footer button names
the number of ticked rows,

V5a-2
00:01:30.963 --> 00:01:32.863
and that is exactly what will be sent.

V5b-1
00:01:33.413 --> 00:01:35.941
Unticking a row is not
the same as reverting it.

V5b-2
00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:38.253
The edit stays in the table for next time.
